{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Planarity on undirected graphs. Self-loops and parallel edges never change an answer: the tests"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run on the underlying simple graph, read once through the rows in index space. A directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph’s planarity is that of "},{"code":"graph.undirectedView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Graph"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isPlanar"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"planarEmbedding()"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isOuterplanar"},{"text":" run the left-right planarity test (de","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Fraysseix and Rosenstiehl, in Brandes’s formulation, 2009); ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"findKuratowskiSubgraph()"},{"text":" runs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Boyer and Myrvold’s edge-addition algorithm (2004), whose failure state isolates the witness.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"All are O(n + m), iterative, and deterministic: graphs with the same rows (the same vertices in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same order, the same edge positions, the same incidence order) get the same embedding and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same witness.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:e:s:14GraphProtocol